cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "K2 and SantanaQAT: how far is 3-bit LLM quantization from the rate-distortion bound? A measurement study, and why the last points are unavailable"
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
type: report
authors:
  - family-names: Mamo
    given-names: Baran
version: k2-3.34bpw-v1
date-released: 2026-10-27
license: CC-BY-4.0
abstract: "A 16x16 tile trellis codec (EXL3/QTIP class) at a 3.34 body bits-per-weight, its runtime for ik_llama.cpp, an SC/RCO per-tensor allocation pipeline, a scales-only QAT (SantanaQAT), and the measurements that bound what 3-bit quantization can reach. Includes the per-item evidence behind every table and the exact allocation that produced the released rate map."
keywords:
  - quantization
  - trellis
  - tcq
  - llm
  - qat
  - gguf
